{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "דבתם רעה", :translit "dibbatam ra'ah", :gloss "their evil report"} {:he "שהם אכלו באבר מן החי", :translit "shehem akhlu be'evar min ha-chai", :gloss "that they ate a limb from a living animal"} {:he "דבתם", :translit "dibbatam", :gloss "their report"} {:he "מות", :translit "mavet", :gloss "death"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "דבתם רעה", :b "שהם אכלו באבר מן החי"} {:kind :gematria, :a "דבתם", :b "מות"}], :frame {:text "The sons of Jacob are said to have committed the sin of eating a limb from a living animal (ever min ha-chai), a prohibition dating to the covenant with Noah (Genesis 9:4). The tradition that lashon ha-ra kills three — the speaker, the listener, and the subject — is found in tractate Arakhin 15b, as cited by Rashi on Numbers 12:1. Ba'al HaTurim compresses both traditions into a single gematria: the numerical value of 'dibbatam ra'ah' equals the phrase about the limb, while 'dibbatam' alone equals 'mavet' (death), encoding the teaching about lashon ha-ra.", :sources ["Genesis 9:4" "Arakhin 15b" "Rashi on Numbers 12:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "נער", :translit "na'ar", :gloss "youth"} {:he "שוטה", :translit "shoteh", :gloss "fool"} {:he "ומוציא דבה הוא כסיל", :translit "u'motzi dibah hu kesil", :gloss "and he who spreads a report is a fool"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "נער", :b "שוטה"}], :frame {:text "The verse 'He who spreads a report is a fool' (Proverbs 10:18) establishes the link between talebearing and folly. By equating 'na'ar' with 'shoteh' in gematria, Ba'al HaTurim reads the description of Joseph as a 'na'ar' as a veiled characterization: Joseph, who brought an evil report about his brothers (Genesis 37:2), is being called a fool in the sense of Proverbs 10:18.", :sources ["Proverbs 10:18" "Genesis 37:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 721, :b-value 720, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "שהם אכלו באבר מן החי", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "דבתם רעה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "דבתם", :a-value 446, :b "מות", :b-value 446, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "נער", :a-value 320, :b "שוטה", :b-value 320, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:16.561563742Z", :model "glm-5.2"}